{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"0cab8709f753a7fde5d3e98531582c083255f0d6eeefa0b64b04d88ef7530abe","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-review batch runner and finalize","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py","src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py","aggregate_usage","_usage","coverage[\"usage\"]","_attach_code_review_metrics","tests/unit/test_code_review_finalize.py"],"problem_keywords":["token usage","incomplete metrics","cloudwatch undercount","pass-1 finder","batch step output"],"propositions":["The code-review Pass-1 finder batch runner does not emit Pass-1 finder token usage on its batch step output, causing the finalize step to omit that usage from CloudWatch totals.","The plan-review side established a convention for surfacing token usage under the _usage key on batch step outputs, which the code-review side must mirror for consistency.","The finalize step already contains folding logic (finalize.py:169-172) to consume _usage from batch step outputs, so only the emit side requires changes.","A unit test must verify that Pass-1 finder token usage is included in the finalized code-review totals, failing before the fix and passing after."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787500691572215001,"uuid":"d6679a71-2ab8-4b94-9f7f-e4b3b6b0bb7e"}